   "source": "# Create comparison chart\nos.makedirs('work/figures', exist_ok=True)\n\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 6))\nx_pos = np.arange(len(metric_names))\nwidth = 0.35\n\nbars1 = ax.bar(x_pos - width/2, baseline_metrics, width, label='Baseline Rule', color='#6c757d', alpha=0.8)\nbars2 = ax.bar(x_pos + width/2, rf_metrics, width, label='Random Forest', color='#4a90d9', alpha=0.8)\n\nax.set_xlabel('Metrics')\nax.set_ylabel('Score')\nax.set_title('Model Performance vs Baseline')\nax.set_xticks(x_pos)\nax.set_xticklabels(metric_names, rotation=45, ha='right')\nax.legend(loc='lower right')\nax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\nax.set_ylim(0, 1)\n\n# Add value labels\nfor bar in bars1:\n    height = bar.get_height()\n    ax.text(bar.get_x() + bar.get_width()/2., height + 0.01,\n            f'{height:.3f}', ha='center', va='bottom', fontsize=9)\nfor bar in bars2:\n    height = bar.get_height()\n    ax.text(bar.get_x() + bar.get_width()/2., height + 0.01,\n            f'{height:.3f}', ha='center', va='bottom', fontsize=9, color='#4a90d9')\n\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.savefig('work/figures/results_comparison.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\nplt.show()\n\nprint(\"\\n✅ Figure saved: work/figures/results_comparison.png\")"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 5. Limitations\n\n*What this work cannot claim.*\n\n### What This Work CAN Claim (Observed/Directional):\n\n- There is a relationship between position and CTR in this dataset\n- Different content types show different CTR patterns\n- Fresher content tends to get more clicks\n- A Random Forest model can predict CTR better than a hand-crafted rule\n\n### What This Work CANNOT Claim:\n\n| Claim | Why Not |\n|-------|---------|\n| \"Position causes higher CTR\" | Correlation ≠ causation |\n| \"This works for all searches\" | Only tested on this dataset |\n| \"Google's algorithm works this way\" | We only observe patterns |\n| \"Perfect prediction\" | The model has errors |\n\n### Practical Limitations\n\n| Limitation | Impact |\n|------------|--------|\n| No search queries | Can't analyze what people search for |\n| No page content | Can't analyze page quality |\n| Aggregated data | Don't see individual user behavior |\n| Limited historical window | Only a few months of data |\n| Google Search Console only | Only Google search data |\n\n### When NOT to Use This Model\n\n1. **High-stakes decisions** - This is decision-support, not a replacement for human judgment\n2. **Causal claims** - Recommendations are directional, not guaranteed\n3. **Pages with <50 impressions** - Predictions may be noisy\n4. **After major algorithm changes** - May need retraining\n5. **For content types not in training** - May not generalize"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "## 6. Ranked recommendations\n\n*The action playbook output — the paper's recommendations section.*"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": "print(\"=\"*60)\nprint(\"RANKED RECOMMENDATIONS\")\nprint(\"=\"*60)\n\n# Create a score column\nif all(col in df.columns for col in ['avg_position', 'content_age_days', 'impressions_90d']):\n    df['score'] = (\n        0.5 * (1 / (df['avg_position'] + 1)) +\n        0.3 * (1 - df['content_age_days'] / 180).clip(0, 1) +\n        0.2 * (df['impressions_90d'] / 1000).clip(0, 1)\n    )\n    df['score'] = df['score'].clip(0, 1)\n\n# Action levels\ndef get_action(score):\n    if score > 0.7:\n        return 'CRITICAL'\n    elif score > 0.55:\n        return 'PRIORITIZE'\n    elif score > 0.4:\n        return 'MONITOR'\n    else:\n        return 'IGNORE'\n\ndf['action'] = df['score'].apply(get_action)\n\n# Reason codes\ndef get_reason(row):\n    reasons = []\n    if row['avg_position'] > 5:\n        reasons.append('POOR_RANK')\n    if row['content_age_days'] > 90:\n        reasons.append('STALE')\n    if row['impressions_90d'] < 100:\n        reasons.append('LOW_VOLUME')\n    return '_'.join(reasons) if reasons else 'OK'\n\ndf['reason_code'] = df.apply(get_reason, axis=1)\n\nprint(\"\\nAction Distribution:\")\nprint(df['action'].value_counts())\n\nprint(\"\\nReason Code Distribution:\")\nprint(df['reason_code'].value_counts().head(10))"
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": "### Action Levels\n\n| Score | Action | Description |\n|-------|--------|-------------|\n| > 0.7 | **CRITICAL** | Immediate content review needed |\n| 0.55-0.7 | **PRIORITIZE** | Content optimization needed |\n| 0.4-0.55 | **MONITOR** | Watch for decline |\n| < 0.4 | **IGNORE** | No action needed |\n\n### Reason Codes\n\n| Code | Meaning | Action |\n|------|---------|--------|\n| `POOR_RANK` | Page ranks poorly (position > 5) | Improve SEO |\n| `STALE` | Content is old (>90 days) | Refresh content |\n| `LOW_VOLUME` | Low impressions (<100) | Boost visibility |\n| `LOW_CTR` | Low CTR (<2%) | Improve content |\n| `OK` | No issues | Maintain current approach |\n\n### Human Review Checklist\n\nBefore acting on any recommendation:\n1. Is the recommendation still relevant?\n2. Does the page have recent changes?\n3. Is this a high-value page?\n4. Are there seasonal factors?\n5. Is the content evergreen or timely?\n\n### What Should NEVER Be Automated\n\n1. Content deletion\n2. Major content rewrite\n3. URL changes\n4. Publishing decisions\n5. Design changes"
  },
