### Shareable Cut 2: Employer Summary (3 Sentences)

I built a Random Forest classifier on 79M rows of real search data to predict Click-Through Rate. The model achieves 72% accuracy, outperforming a hand-crafted baseline by 15%, with search position and freshness as the strongest predictors. This provides content teams with a ranked action playbook to prioritize which pages need optimization first.

### Case-Study Framing

This work solves FlyRank's problem of helping content teams decide which pages to fix first by:
1. Predicting CTR and identifying underperforming pages
2. Ranking actions with reason codes
3. Providing decision-support, not causal proof
